---
import "../../styles/cifro.css";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout variant="cifro" title="Cifro Support: help with the iPhone budget app" description="Cifro support: how to contact me, where your data lives, iCloud sync, currencies, Face ID and supported iPhones." favicon="/cifro/icon.jpg">
  <section class="page-intro compact"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Cifro</p><h1>Cifro support</h1><p>Questions about <a href="/cifro/">Cifro</a>? Email me and I'll answer.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section tint"><div class="shell prose"><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:me@alesanabriav.com?subject=Cifro%20support">me@alesanabriav.com</a> with the Cifro version, your iPhone model, and a short description of what happened. Do not include personal financial information.</p>
  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <p><strong>Where is my data?</strong> Cifro keeps its data on your iPhone. Deleting the app may remove locally stored app data, so check your device backup settings before uninstalling if you need to keep it.</p>
  <p><strong>How does sync work?</strong> Sync is optional and goes through your own private iCloud account. There is no Cifro account.</p>
  <p><strong>Can I use other currencies?</strong> Yes. Choose your main currency and log expenses in others. Cifro converts them with current exchange rates, which is the only thing it fetches from the internet.</p>
  <p><strong>Can I lock the app?</strong> Yes, with Face ID or Touch ID.</p>
  <p><strong>Which iPhones are supported?</strong> iPhone with iOS 26 or later. Cifro AI needs an iPhone that supports Apple Intelligence.</p>
  <h2>Privacy</h2><p>Read the <a href="/cifro/privacy/">Cifro privacy policy</a>.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
